    <paragraph>Use Logarithmic Models in Applications</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use a logarithmic model to solve.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="208" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>What is the decibel level of normal conversation with intensity $$10^{-6}$$ watts per square inch?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="209" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>What is the decibel level of a whisper with intensity $$10^{-10}$$ watts per square inch?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>A whisper has a decibel level of 20 dB.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="210" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>What is the decibel level of the noise from a motorcycle with intensity $$10^{-2}$$ watts per square inch?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="211" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>What is the decibel level of the sound of a garbage disposal with intensity $$10^{-2}$$ watts per square inch?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>The sound of a garbage disposal has a decibel level of 100 dB.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="212" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>In 2014, Chile experienced an intense earthquake with a magnitude of $$8.2$$ on the Richter scale. In 2010, Haiti also experienced an intense earthquake which measured $$7.0$$ on the Richter scale. Compare the intensities of the two earthquakes.</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="213" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>The Los Angeles area experiences many earthquakes. In 1994, the Northridge earthquake measured magnitude of $$6.7$$ on the Richter scale. In 2014, Los Angeles also experienced an earthquake which measured $$5.1$$ on the Richter scale. Compare the intensities of the two earthquakes.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>The intensity of the 1994 Northridge earthquake in the Los Angeles area was about 40 times the intensity of the 2014 earthquake.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
